---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy notice" description="What nextgenergy.ai collects, which is very little, and how to reach us about it.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Company" title="Privacy notice" lede="This site is built to collect as little as possible. Here is exactly what happens when you visit, what happens when you write to us, and how to have anything removed." crumbs={[['/company/about', 'Company']]} />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>When you visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics, and what “Decline” does.</strong> Google Analytics runs in Consent Mode with all advertising features disabled. The Google tag loads on every page whatever you choose. Before you choose, and after you click “Decline”, analytics cookies stay off (any existing <code>_ga</code> cookies are deleted when you decline), but the tag still sends Google one cookieless measurement request per page view. That request carries the page address and title, browser, language and screen details, and a temporary identifier that is not stored on your device; Google uses such requests for aggregate, modelled reporting. Declining therefore stops cookie-based tracking, not all measurement. If you click “Accept analytics”, Google may also set analytics cookies such as <code>_ga</code> to recognise repeat visits. You can change your choice at any time using “Analytics choices” in the footer. To send nothing to Google at all, block <code>googletagmanager.com</code> and <code>google-analytics.com</code> with a content blocker or your browser's tracking protection; the site works without them.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting logs.</strong> The site is served by Cloudflare. Like any web server, Cloudflare's edge records standard request logs (IP address, requested page, browser type, timestamp) for security and operations. We do not receive these as personal data and do not use them to identify visitors. Cloudflare's own privacy policy applies to that processing.</li>
        <li><strong>Fonts and stylesheets</strong> are served from this domain. Apart from the optional Google Analytics tag above, no script is loaded from a third party.</li>
        <li><strong>Images in articles</strong> under /insights are loaded from Substack's content network (substackcdn.com), because those articles are mirrored from our Substack publication. Loading an image sends a standard request, including your IP address, to Substack.</li>
        <li><strong>The turnover self-check tool</strong> stores your tick marks in your own browser (local storage) so they survive a reload. Nothing is sent to us. Clearing your browser data removes it.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>When you write to us</h2>
      <p>The contact form sends your name, organisation, email, topic, message and any optional project details you fill in over HTTPS to our server, which forwards them as an email to {site.email}. The server does not store them. If the form cannot send, the page tells you the message was not delivered and offers our address, a copy of your message and an optional draft for your own email app; nothing is sent until you send it yourself. What we receive is an ordinary email, which we keep in our company mailbox (Google Workspace) for as long as the enquiry and any resulting relationship is active. We use it to reply to you and for nothing else. We do not sell, rent or share enquiry details with third parties.</p>
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>To have an email and its contents deleted, write to {site.email} and say so. We will confirm when it is done. If you are in the EU, UK or Canada you have the rights those jurisdictions give you over personal data, including access and erasure, and you may exercise them through the same address.</p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If we add any further third-party service that processes visitor data, this page will be updated first and the change will be dated here.</p>
      <p class="small muted">Last updated 2 October 2026 (what “Decline” does, stated from the tag's observed behaviour; contact form failure handling). Contact for this notice: {site.email}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
